<!--
  ============================================================================
  HomesteadDefenseLeague.xml              Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  Builds FACTION_SPEC.md section 3, "Homestead Defense League ; PATCH vanilla
  `OutlanderCivil`". A reskin, not a new def.

  READ FROM THE SHIPPED DEF, 2026-08-14 ; not inferred:
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Core\Defs\
    FactionDefs\Factions_Misc.xml

      ParentName                  OutlanderFactionBase
      OWN nodes                   defName · label · description · colorSpectrum ·
                                  classicIdeo · maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation ·
                                  configurationListOrderPriority
      label                       civil outlander union

  🔴 EVERYTHING ELSE IS ON THE ABSTRACT PARENT, NOT ON THIS DEF.
  `OutlanderFactionBase` is where `pawnSingular`, `pawnsPlural`, `leaderTitle`
  and `settlementGenerationWeight` actually live. PatchOperations run BEFORE
  def inheritance is resolved, so at patch time `OutlanderCivil` literally does
  not have those nodes. A `Replace` on any of them matches ZERO and logs red.
  They are `Add`s onto the child, and the child's own node wins at inheritance
  time, which is exactly the override we want and reaches `OutlanderCivil`
  ALONE ; patching the parent would also hit OutlanderRough and every modded
  descendant.

      pawnSingular / pawnsPlural  parent      ->  Add
      leaderTitle                 parent      ->  Add
      settlementGenerationWeight  parent (1)  ->  Add
      raidsForbidden              ABSENT in the whole chain  ->  Add
      label / description         own nodes   ->  Replace

  🔴 SUPERSEDED 2026-08-21 === OUTLANDER_GROUPMAKER_PATCH_1, owner: "Approved
  abstract patch." This file used to say `pawnGroupMakers` was untouched. It no
  longer is: four ADDITIVE group makers now hang off the abstract parent at the
  end of this file, because the League's five authored pawn kinds were reachable
  by nobody. `factionNameMaker` and the raid curves ARE still untouched, and
  vanilla's own group makers and option weights are not edited at all.
  (`fixedName` was added 2026-08-21 too === FACTION_FIXEDNAME_ELEVEN_1.)

  ⚠️ `raidsForbidden` is the MECHANISM for R2, not a precept. It is what makes
  the League never raid the player, and it has no vanilla default here.

  ✅ The ideo layer (`fixedIdeo` / `ideoName` "the Covenant of Free Wells" /
  `deityPresets`) IS in this file, at the end of the sequence. It was going to
  land in a separate `FactionReligions.xml`; it did not, and keeping the faith
  beside the faction it belongs to is the arrangement that stands.
  `deityPresets/li` takes `nameType` (`name` + `type`), `gender` and `iconPath` —
  read off `DeityPreset` and `DeityNameType`, not guessed.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Everything sits inside a conditional on the def existing, so the file is a
  silent no-op rather than a wall of red if the vessel ever moves. One defName
  here is not Core - `AM_WaterPrimacy`, which carries `MayRequire="sarg.alphamemes"`.
  The Ideology memes are left bare, which is the house convention across every
  faction file: the DLC is in the frozen list and the whole ideo block is inert
  without it, so the exposure is a red line at load, not wrong behaviour.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- "civil outlander union" -> the campaign name. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Homestead Defense League</label></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>The most numerous and least centralised faction on the world — farmers on the dry flats, living off whatever their vaporators pull out of the night air.\n\nDecent, tired, and badly armed. They defend wells and they do not come looking for anyone.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Inherited from OutlanderFactionBase. Add, not Replace. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><pawnSingular>moisture farmer</pawnSingular></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><pawnsPlural>moisture farmers</pawnsPlural></value>
        </li>

        <!-- "prime councilor" on the parent -> High Marshal. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><leaderTitle>High Marshal</leaderTitle></value>
        </li>

        <!-- R2's mechanism. Absent throughout the chain, so this creates it. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><raidsForbidden>true</raidsForbidden></value>
        </li>

        <!-- 1 on the parent -> 1.9. Thirteen settlements, the most on the map. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><settlementGenerationWeight>1.9</settlementGenerationWeight></value>
        </li>

        <!--
          ================================================================
          faction_religions_spec.md entry 3 (B54)
          ================================================================
          `ideoName` and `ideoDescription` verbatim; they are the only strings
          the engine renders. ⛔ `hiddenIdeo` MUST STAY UNSET or the
          description is never shown. Structure meme goes FIRST in
          `forcedMemes`.

          `OutlanderCivil` ships `classicIdeo true`. It is removed: an authored
          `fixedIdeo` is not the classic single-ideo mode, and vanilla's only
          `fixedIdeo` def (HoraxCult) carries neither that nor `disallowedMemes`.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]/classicIdeo</xpath>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
            <requiredPreceptsOnly>false</requiredPreceptsOnly>
            <ideoName>the Covenant of Free Wells</ideoName>
            <ideoDescription>Water was given once and the Giver stepped back, and we have not been spoken to since. That is not abandonment. It is the test. A well belongs to whoever is thirsty standing at it — we have never turned a stranger away, and we have buried our own for it. We do not take up arms and go out. We stand on our own ground, we keep the vaporators turning, and we answer to the silence.</ideoDescription>
            <forcedMemes>
              <li>Structure_TheistAbstract</li>
              <li MayRequire="sarg.alphamemes">AM_WaterPrimacy</li>
              <li>Individualist</li>
              <li>Guilty</li>
              <li>Rancher</li>
            </forcedMemes>
            <deityPresets>
              <li>
                <nameType><name>the Withdrawn</name><type>That Which Was Given</type></nameType>
                <gender>None</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/DeityGeneric</iconPath>
              </li>
            </deityPresets>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Bespoke world-map icon. the def does NOT write it - it inherits Expanding/Town from OutlanderFactionBase, so ADD.
             A Replace here would match nothing and log nothing. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><factionIconPath>World/JawaFactions/HomesteadLeague</factionIconPath></value>
        </li>

        <!-- The name the world object carries. No vanilla FactionDef writes fixedName
             (checked in Core/Defs/FactionDefs/Factions_Misc.xml), so this is an ADD.
             A Replace would match nothing and log red. factionNameMaker stays: it still
             names this faction's SETTLEMENTS. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><fixedName>Homestead Defense League</fixedName></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!--
    ========================================================================
    THE FIVE KINDS GET SOMEWHERE TO BE USED === OUTLANDER_GROUPMAKER_PATCH_1
    ========================================================================
    🔴 OWNER, 2026-08-21: "Approved abstract patch." This reverses the ⛔ in the
    header of this file and closes what
    `sixteen-roster-kinds-have-nowhere-to-be-used-8f21c4` was waiting on.

    `pawnGroupMakers` for this faction is NOT on `OutlanderCivil`. It is on the
    abstract parent `OutlanderFactionBase`
    (Core/Defs/FactionDefs/Factions_Misc.xml), so every earlier xpath at
    `FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]/pawnGroupMakers` matched ZERO and
    logged nothing. That silent failure is what this operation ends. The parent is
    abstract, so it is addressed by its `Name` ATTRIBUTE, not by a defName.

    Reachable by nobody until now, all five authored in
    `Defs/PawnKindDefs/JawaFactionRoster.xml`:
      Jawa_Homestead_Grunt · _Heavy · _Specialist · _Leader · _DesertRanger

    ⚠️ THIS REACHES EVERY OUTLANDER FACTION, not just the League. That is the
    accepted cost of the approval, and the reason the weights are what they are.
    ADDITIVE ONLY: four NEW `<li>` group makers are appended. ⛔ Not one vanilla
    `<li>`, option or weight is edited, removed or reweighted.

    THE NUMBER, because the item asks for a number and not an assertion.
    `PawnGroupMaker.commonality` defaults to 100 (read off the class, not
    assumed) and every vanilla Outlander group maker leaves it unset. At
    commonality 5 each new group maker takes 5/(100+5) = 4.8% of the groups of
    its kind; 95.2% of ordinary Outlander groups are composed exactly as before,
    and the ones that are not still field ordinary humans with faction xenotypes.

    ⭐ The dune ranger carries the joint-highest weight in every group it is in.
    It is the one that must actually be SEEN, because it is the only one of the
    five dressed explicitly (duster + headwrap, both Core).

    Group kinds used: Combat · Peaceful · Trader · Settlement. The League is
    `raidsForbidden`, so Peaceful and Trader are where the player actually meets
    it; Combat and Settlement are for its settlement being attacked and for its
    Outlander cousins.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[@Name="OutlanderFactionBase"]/pawnGroupMakers</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[@Name="OutlanderFactionBase"]/pawnGroupMakers</xpath>
      <value>

        <li>
          <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
          <commonality>5</commonality>
          <options>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Grunt>10</Jawa_Homestead_Grunt>
            <Jawa_Homestead_DesertRanger>10</Jawa_Homestead_DesertRanger>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Heavy>6</Jawa_Homestead_Heavy>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Specialist>4</Jawa_Homestead_Specialist>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Leader>1</Jawa_Homestead_Leader>
          </options>
        </li>

        <li>
          <kindDef>Peaceful</kindDef>
          <commonality>5</commonality>
          <options>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Grunt>10</Jawa_Homestead_Grunt>
            <Jawa_Homestead_DesertRanger>10</Jawa_Homestead_DesertRanger>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Heavy>4</Jawa_Homestead_Heavy>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Specialist>4</Jawa_Homestead_Specialist>
          </options>
        </li>

        <!-- `traders` and `carriers` repeat vanilla's own because a Trader group
             cannot generate without a trader kind; only the GUARDS are ours. -->
        <li>
          <kindDef>Trader</kindDef>
          <commonality>5</commonality>
          <traders>
            <Town_Trader>1</Town_Trader>
          </traders>
          <carriers>
            <Dromedary>10</Dromedary>
            <Muffalo>3</Muffalo>
            <Alpaca>2</Alpaca>
          </carriers>
          <guards>
            <Jawa_Homestead_DesertRanger>10</Jawa_Homestead_DesertRanger>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Grunt>8</Jawa_Homestead_Grunt>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Heavy>6</Jawa_Homestead_Heavy>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Specialist>3</Jawa_Homestead_Specialist>
          </guards>
        </li>

        <li>
          <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
          <commonality>5</commonality>
          <options>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Grunt>10</Jawa_Homestead_Grunt>
            <Jawa_Homestead_DesertRanger>10</Jawa_Homestead_DesertRanger>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Heavy>8</Jawa_Homestead_Heavy>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Specialist>5</Jawa_Homestead_Specialist>
            <Jawa_Homestead_Leader>2</Jawa_Homestead_Leader>
          </options>
        </li>

      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ═══ LEADER_TITLES_ON_THE_IDEO_1, 2026-08-22 ═══════════════════════════════
       `Faction.LeaderTitle` (RimWorld/Faction.cs:142) prefers the primary IDEO's
       `leaderTitleMale` and only falls back to `def.leaderTitle`. Measured live:
       the ideo overrode the def on 36 of 37 factions, so the Homestead Defense League's authored
       title "High Marshal" was never the word a player read. The ideo's title is
       generated from its CULTURE's `leaderTitleMaker`, so the route is a culture
       of our own - full mechanism in `Defs/CultureDefs/JawaLeaderTitles.xml`.
       ⛔ Not a patch on the shared vanilla culture: Rustican is shared with every
       faction of its category in 578 mods and patching it renames all of them.
       ⚠️ This BAKES at world creation and cannot be retrofitted. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
      <value><allowedCultures Inherit="False"><li>Jawa_Culture_Homestead</li></allowedCultures></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
